<Item XName="Notes" UserName="Notes" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Oscillator Phase Lock Loop Design and Performance&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Workspace&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;This is a template that sets up a phase lock loop (PLL) for a noisy RF oscillator by phase locking it a low noise crystal oscillator and shows the PLL loop filter response, PLL step response, PLL closed loop swept frequency response, and reduction of the noisy oscillator noise that is close in to the carrier within the defined PLL closed loop bandwidth.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-outline-level: 3&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;PLL Design Setup: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The design is set up by setting variables in the Equation1 sheet.&amp;nbsp; The design is for a 2nd order phase type 1 phase lock loop.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In the Equation1 page set these RF parameters:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;RF_Freq = the RF oscillator frequency.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;DivN =&amp;nbsp;the frequency divider integer value.&amp;nbsp; The reference crystal oscillator will have the frequency RF_Freq/DivN.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;In the Equation1 page set these control loop parameters:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;BW = Closed loop bandwidth in Hz.&lt;BR&gt;NZ = Normalized zero for the PLL.&lt;BR&gt;DF =&amp;nbsp;Damping factor&amp;nbsp;for the PLL.&lt;BR&gt;PDGC =&amp;nbsp;Phase detector gain constant, volts/deg&lt;BR&gt;KV =&amp;nbsp;VCO tuning sensitivity, Hz/volt&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Once these values are set the rest of the simulations are set up automatically.&amp;nbsp; This includes the simulation sample rate and stop time.&amp;nbsp; The number of simulation points is preset to 2^12.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The Equation1 sheet also shows derived 2nd order PLL responses based on PLL theory.&amp;nbsp; These theoretical PLL responses include:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL type=disc&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;BWn = Closed loop noise bandwidth, Hz&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;FP = closed loop frequency for maximum gain, Hz&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;AP_dB =&amp;nbsp;maximum closed loop gain in dB at frequency FP&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;PO = Step response percent overshoot&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list .5in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Tmax =&amp;nbsp;Step response time to maximum overshoot&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The preset design is set with:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;RF_Freq = 320 MHz&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;DivN = 8;&amp;nbsp; this implies that the crystal oscillator is at 40 MHz.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;BW = 100 Hz.&lt;BR&gt;NZ = 1.&lt;BR&gt;DF =&amp;nbsp;1/sqrt(2).&lt;BR&gt;PDGC =&amp;nbsp;0.1*pi/180&lt;BR&gt;KV =&amp;nbsp;BW&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Loop Filter Response: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;With the PLL Design Setup defined above,&amp;nbsp;the resultant loop filter response is evaluated.&amp;nbsp; See the folder &apos;Loop Filter Response&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The design is &apos;LoopFilter_test&apos; with associated analysis and data &apos;LoopFilter_Analysis&apos; and &apos;LoopFilter_Data&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;This PLL loop filter pole and zero frequencies are designed based on the PLL specifications for BW, DF, and NZ.&amp;nbsp; Additionally, the gain of the loop filter is defined based on the amount of gain external to this filter.&amp;nbsp; The loop filter is a subnetwork model named LoopFilter with parameters NormalizedZero, DampingFactor, BW and ExternalGain.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The preset design values for NormalizedZero, DampingFactor, and BW are shown above.&amp;nbsp; The present value for ExternalGain is derived in the Equation1 page as variable ExtG.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The loop filter gain versus frequency is shown in graph &apos;LoopFilter_Gain_vs_Freq&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;For the preset values, the loop filter has a low frequency gain of 41.8 dB, a pole at about 15 Hz, a zero at about 150 Hz and a high frequency gain of 34.2 dB.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Note that though the closed loop bandwidth, BW, is preset to 100 Hz, the required loop filter pole is about 15 Hz.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;PLL Step&amp;nbsp;Response: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;With the PLL Design Setup defined above,&amp;nbsp;the resultant loop step response is evaluated.&amp;nbsp; See the folder &apos;PLL Step Response&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The design is &apos;PLL_StepResponse&apos; with associated analysis and data &apos;StepResp_Analysis&apos; and &apos;StepResp_Data&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The PLL design is defined to control the oscillator/modulator combination with instance names RF_Osc and RF_Osc_Modulator.&amp;nbsp; The RF_Osc is&amp;nbsp;operating at frequency RF_Freq defined in the Equation1 page &amp;nbsp;is an input to the RF_Osc_Modulator.&amp;nbsp; The output of the RF_Osc_Modulator is routed to a frequency divider, FreqMpyDiv, with frequency division ratio DivN defined in the Equation1 page.&amp;nbsp; The FreqMpyDiv output is an input to the PhaseComparator whose other input is from another Modulator that serves as the PLL reference signal at frequency RF_Freq/DivN.&amp;nbsp; This reference Modulator has a frequency step applied to its as a square wave at its frequency control input.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;As the reference oscillator frequency has a step in frequency, the PLL will drive the RF_Osc_Modulator to have the same frequency step, but with dynamics controlled by the PLL Design Setup defined above.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The loop step response&amp;nbsp;is shown in graph &apos;Step_Response&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;For the preset values, the Equation1 page shows that the theoretical step percent overshoot (PO) expected is 10.7% and the time at which the peak overshoot is expected is at 5.9e-3 sec.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;From the&amp;nbsp;graph &apos;Step_Response&apos;, the simulated percent overshoot is 11.4% and the time at which the peak overshoot occurs is at 6.0e-3 sec.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Thus, the simulated PLL step response performance agrees quite closely to the expected theoretical values.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;PLL Swept Freq&amp;nbsp;Response: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;With the PLL Design Setup defined above,&amp;nbsp;the resultant&amp;nbsp;closed loop frequency response is evaluated.&amp;nbsp; See the folder &apos;PLL Swept Freq Response&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The design is &apos;PLL_FreqResponse&apos; with associated analysis and data &apos;FreqResp_Analysis&apos; and &apos;FreqResp_Data&apos; and associated sweep and data &apos;Sweep1&apos; and &apos;Sweep1_Data&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The PLL design is essentially the same as the one defined in the PLL_StepResponse design, but with a swept sinusoid modulating the frequency of the reference modulator instead of a frequency step.&amp;nbsp; The sinusoid frequency is defined by variable FNom in the Equation2 page.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The swept sinusoid is achieved by use of the Sweep1 evaluation which sweeps the sinusoid frequency logarithmically from FNomStart to FNomStop.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The Equation2 sheet is used to set FNom.&amp;nbsp; It typically is set to a value within the loop bandwidth.&amp;nbsp; BW/10 is the recommended value.&amp;nbsp; This value needs to be manually set by the user since SystemVue does not allow FNom to be set to an expression if it is to be tuned and used in the Sweep1.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The Equation3 sheet contains functions used in the Equation2 and Equation3 sheets.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The Equation4 sheet contains expressions that extract the closed loop frequency response from the Sweep1_Data.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The closed loop frequency response is&amp;nbsp;shown in graph &apos;ClosedLoop_SweptFreqResponse&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;For the preset values, the Equation1 page shows that the theoretical closed loop frequency which&amp;nbsp;has the maximum amplitude (FP) is expected to be 41.4 Hz and this occurs with maximum amplitude (AP_dB) expected as 0.8 dB.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;From the&amp;nbsp;graph &apos;ClosedLoop_SweptFreqResponse&apos;, the simulated maximum closed loop frequency is&amp;nbsp;41.7 Hz and this has the maximum amplitude of 0.9 dB.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;Thus, the simulated PLL closed loop frequency response performance agrees quite closely to the expected theoretical values.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;PLL Osc Noise&amp;nbsp;Response: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;With the PLL Design Setup defined above,&amp;nbsp;and with the PLL design verified in the tests for &apos;Loop Filter Response&apos;, &apos;PLL Step Response&apos; and &apos;PLL Swept Freq Response&apos;, a noise oscillator at frequency RF_Freq can be used in a PLL with a low noise reference oscillator at RF_Freq/8 to clean up the RF_Freq noise close in to the carrier within the PLL closed loop 3dB bandwidth (BW). &amp;nbsp;See the folder &apos;PLL Osc Noise&amp;nbsp;Response&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The design is &apos;PLL_Osc_Response&apos; with associated analysis and data &apos;PLL_Osc_Analysis&apos; and &apos;PLL_Osc_Data&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The PLL design is essentially the same as the one defined in the PLL_StepResponse design, but with a constant low noise oscillator at RF_Freq/DivN used as the reference oscillator for the RF_Freq oscillator/modulator.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The RF_Freq oscillator is defined with phase noise.&amp;nbsp; The objective of the PLL is to clean up the close in phase noise within the closed loop bandwidth.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The oscillator RF spectrums are&amp;nbsp;shown in graph &apos;PLL_Osc_SpecOutRF_Power&apos;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The blue curve is the RF spectrum for the original RF_Freq oscillator.&amp;nbsp; Note the phase noise about the RF carrier, especially close in to the carrier.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The red curve is the RF spectrum with the PLL applied and referenced to the low noise oscillator.&amp;nbsp; Note that the phase noise is reduced close to the RF carrier within the defined closed loop bandwidth.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;LINE-HEIGHT: normal; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;The graph &apos;PLL_SpecOut_Power&apos; shows the single sided spectrum with the carrier at DC.&amp;nbsp; This graph shows more clearly the noise reduction due to the use of the PLL and low noise oscillator.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot; class=MsoNormal&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
